    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-37394",
      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-8)|\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-4)|\\begin{aligned}3 & 8-\\lambda  \\\\ -6 & -10\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +6)+8(-3\\lambda +9)-4(-6\\lambda +18) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6)+(-24\\lambda +72)-(-24\\lambda +72) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
      "grade": "Correct",
